     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">​I got the same when I did a &quot;load()&quot; function. I tried to directly use the &quot;readRDS()&quot; function but got weird error messages. But the following code _seemed_ to work OK for me:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&gt; download.file(&quot;<a href=\"http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367319111000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ylehiNExVHpd3p7PnnW88\">http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds</a>&quot;,&quot;temp.rds&quot;)</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">trying URL &#39;<a href=\"http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367319111000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ylehiNExVHpd3p7PnnW88\">http://biogeo.ucdavis.edu/data/gadm2.8/rds/TUR_adm0.rds</a>&#39;</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Content type &#39;unknown&#39; length 678858 bytes (662 KB)</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">==================================================</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">downloaded 662 KB</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&gt; turkey=readRDS(&quot;temp.rds&quot;)</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&gt; unlink(&quot;temp.rds&quot;)</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">This required that I install a package called &quot;sp&quot;. Apparently that is some plotting package. I&#39;d never heard of it before. The command &quot;spplot(turkey)&quot; created a rather ugly looking graphic. Most like that is due to my ignorance of the &quot;sp&quot; package.​</div><br></div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div style=\"font-family:timesnewromanpsmt\"><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">Regards,</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">Serdar</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=